+(duration-opts)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a string into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. It accepts either a whole number of
+seconds, or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups using the units `d`, `h`, `m` and `s`. Each unit may be used at most
+once, in that order, without spaces. Units are case-insensitive.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration())
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(timeout)
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=5w'])
+```
+
